(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct Edward de Bono's 'Six Thinking Hats' methodology. Analyze the specific cognitive mode and emotional discipline required for each of the six colored hats.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Conceptual Philosophy of Six Thinking Hats:) Tj
T*
(   - Developed by Edward de Bono, the framework separates thinking into six distinct, parallel) Tj
T*
(   cognitive modes. Instead of chaotic debate where egos clash, all participants don the same) Tj
T*
(   colored hat simultaneously, looking in the exact same direction together.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Cognitive Mode & Discipline per Hat:) Tj
T*
(   - White Hat \(Objective Data\): Neutral, objective, and factual. Focuses exclusively on) Tj
T*
(   verifiable figures, available metrics, historical data, and information gaps. No) Tj
T*
(   interpretations, opinions, or emotional coloring permitted.) Tj
T*
(   - Red Hat \(Emotions & Intuition\): Pure gut feeling, hunch, and affective reaction. Participants) Tj
T*
(   express their intuitive feelings without needing to provide any logical justification or) Tj
T*
(   apology \('I feel this partnership is treacherous'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Black Hat \(Caution & Risk Evaluation\): Critical judgment and logical pessimism. Identifies) Tj
T*
(   fatal flaws, compliance violations, security risks, budget overruns, and failure modes. Must be) Tj
T*
(   grounded in logical reasons, not vague negativity.) Tj
T*
(   - Yellow Hat \(Logical Optimism\): Constructive positivity and feasibility. Explores benefits,) Tj
T*
(   potential value, scalability advantages, and how ideas can be made workable. Requires logical) Tj
T*
(   grounding, not blind wishful thinking.) Tj
T*
(   - Green Hat \(Creativity & Provocation\): Lateral leaps, out-of-the-box alternatives, wild ideas,) Tj
T*
(   and provocative propositions \(PO\). Judgment is completely suspended to allow radical) Tj
T*
(   exploration.) Tj
T*
(   - Blue Hat \(Process & Metacognition\): Orchestration and facilitation. Defines the agenda,) Tj
T*
(   selects the hat sequence, monitors time, enforces discipline, and synthesizes conclusions and) Tj
T*
(   action items.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Illustrate the application of the 'Six Thinking Hats' framework to a high-stakes engineering crisis: deciding whether to roll back or patch forward a mission-critical cloud deployment during a live outage.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Incident Context:) Tj
T*
(   - A major fintech payment gateway deployment introduces an unexpected thread deadlock, causing) Tj
T*
(   15% of live transactions to fail. The engineering leadership gathers to decide whether to roll) Tj
T*
(   back to the previous version or patch forward in production.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Structured Hat Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   - Blue Hat \(Opening - 2 mins\): Facilitator states the goal: 'We have 15 minutes to reach an) Tj
T*
ET

