(   [Problem Statement]: Construct a formal 'Pugh Matrix' to evaluate three competing container orchestration technologies \(Kubernetes, Docker Swarm, Nomad\) against a baseline legacy virtual machine architecture.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Pugh Matrix Selection Methodology:) Tj
T*
(   - Developed by Stuart Pugh, this matrix evaluates alternative concepts against a established) Tj
T*
(   baseline reference across multi-dimensional criteria using relative scoring:) Tj
T*
(   * '+' = Concept performs significantly better than baseline.) Tj
T*
(   * '-' = Concept performs significantly worse than baseline.) Tj
T*
(   * 'S' or '0' = Concept performs identically to baseline.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Matrix Construction \(Baseline = Legacy Virtual Machines on VMware\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Criteria | Weight | Baseline \(VMs\) | Kubernetes | Docker Swarm | Nomad) Tj
T*
(   -------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(   Deployment Velocity | 25% | 0 \(Baseline\) | + \(+2\) | + \(+1\) | + \(+2\)) Tj
T*
(   High Availability/Auto | 20% | 0 \(Baseline\) | + \(+2\) | + \(+1\) | + \(+2\)) Tj
T*
(   Operational Simplicity | 20% | 0 \(Baseline\) | - \(-2\) | + \(+2\) | + \(+1\)) Tj
T*
(   Ecosystem & Community | 15% | 0 \(Baseline\) | + \(+2\) | - \(-1\) | S \(0\)) Tj
T*
(   Multi-Cloud Portability | 10% | 0 \(Baseline\) | + \(+2\) | + \(+1\) | + \(+2\)) Tj
T*
(   Resource Efficiency | 10% | 0 \(Baseline\) | + \(+2\) | + \(+1\) | + \(+2\)) Tj
T*
(   -------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(   Weighted Score Sum: | 0.00 | +1.20 | +0.95 | +1.35) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Synthesis and Decision Rationale:) Tj
T*
