(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the 'MoSCoW' prioritization framework. Establish rigorous architectural boundary criteria for determining whether an engineering requirement is a 'Must Have' versus a 'Should Have'.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Taxonomy of MoSCoW:) Tj
T*
(   - Must Have \(M\): Absolute non-negotiable core functionality. Without it, the product cannot) Tj
T*
(   launch, violates legal regulations, or provides zero utility.) Tj
T*
(   - Should Have \(S\): Highly critical functionality that is expected in a competitive product, but) Tj
T*
(   can be temporarily omitted if time expires because a viable workaround exists.) Tj
T*
(   - Could Have \(C\): Desirable enhancements and minor features that are included only if surplus) Tj
T*
(   development bandwidth remains.) Tj
T*
(   - Won't Have \(W\): Explicitly agreed out-of-scope features for this release cycle, preserved for) Tj
T*
(   future roadmap iterations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Rigorous Boundary Criteria \(Must vs. Should\):) Tj
T*
(   - Legal & Regulatory Compliance: If missing the feature exposes the company to criminal fines) Tj
T*
(   or lawsuit shutdowns \(e.g., GDPR data deletion API, HIPAA audit logs\), it is strictly a MUST) Tj
T*
(   HAVE. If it is merely an industry best-practice guideline, it is a SHOULD HAVE.) Tj
T*
(   - System Viability & Operational Integrity: If the system cannot complete its primary) Tj
T*
(   end-to-end transaction without human intervention \(e.g., credit card payment gateway) Tj
T*
(   integration\), it is a MUST HAVE. If an automated refund wizard fails, but customer support can) Tj
T*
(   issue manual refunds via an admin portal, it is a SHOULD HAVE.) Tj
T*
(   - Workaround Feasibility: If no viable workaround exists, it is a MUST. If a human procedural) Tj
T*
(   workaround exists that is acceptable for 30 days, it is downgraded to a SHOULD.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Schedule Protection:) Tj
T*
(   - To prevent catastrophic release delays, engineering releases must cap Must Haves at a maximum) Tj
T*
(   of 60% of total team sprint capacity, reserving 40% for Should/Could buffers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
