(   1. Foundations of Analogous Inspiration:) Tj
T*
(   - Breakthrough innovation occurs when engineers map abstract architectural patterns from a) Tj
T*
(   mature, non-digital domain onto an unresolved digital challenge, bypassing domain-specific) Tj
T*
(   dogma.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Postal Delivery Service Analogy for Packet Switching \(Paul Baran, Vint Cerf\):) Tj
T*
(   - The Legacy Telecom Telephony Mental Model: Circuit switching. A telephone call created a) Tj
T*
(   continuous, dedicated physical copper wire connection from end to end. If a single cable) Tj
T*
(   snapped, the entire call dropped. It was horribly inefficient and fragile during nuclear) Tj
T*
(   strikes.) Tj
T*
(   - The Analogous Inspiration: The Postal System:) Tj
T*
(   * In the mail system, no dedicated truck drives a single letter directly from sender to) Tj
T*
(   receiver.) Tj
T*
(   * Letters are placed in standard envelopes with uniform sender and recipient addresses \(IP) Tj
T*
(   Packets with Headers\).) Tj
T*
(   * Envelopes are passed through a series of sorting facilities \(Routers\), routed along whichever) Tj
T*
(   path is currently available.) Tj
T*
(   * If a large book must be sent, it can be mailed as individual chapters in separate numbered) Tj
T*
(   envelopes, reassembled by the receiver upon arrival \(TCP Packet Reassembly and Sequence) Tj
T*
(   Numbers\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Engineering Triumph of TCP/IP:) Tj
T*
(   - Packet switching made the internet radically resilient; individual packet streams dynamically) Tj
T*
(   route around destroyed physical fiber nodes, revolutionizing global communications.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
