(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the 'Kano Model' mapping of customer preferences. Detail how an engineering team uses Kano questionnaires \(Functional vs. Dysfunctional\) to classify features.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Kano Analytical Framework:) Tj
T*
(   - Maps functionality against customer satisfaction across five categories: Must-be \(M\),) Tj
T*
(   One-dimensional \(O\), Attractive \(A\), Indifferent \(I\), and Reverse \(R\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Functional vs. Dysfunctional Questionnaire Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - For every prospective feature, the user is asked two paired questions with 5 standardized) Tj
T*
(   Likert responses \(1: I like it; 2: I expect it; 3: I am neutral; 4: I can tolerate it; 5: I) Tj
T*
(   dislike it\):) Tj
T*
(   * Functional Question: 'How do you feel if this feature is PRESENT in the software?') Tj
T*
(   * Dysfunctional Question: 'How do you feel if this feature is ABSENT from the software?') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Kano Classification Evaluation Matrix:) Tj
T*
(   - If User says:) Tj
T*
(   * Functional: 'I expect it' AND Dysfunctional: 'I dislike it' -> MUST-BE \(Basic threshold\).) Tj
T*
(   * Functional: 'I like it' AND Dysfunctional: 'I dislike it' -> ONE-DIMENSIONAL \(Linear) Tj
T*
(   performance\).) Tj
T*
(   * Functional: 'I like it' AND Dysfunctional: 'I am neutral' -> ATTRACTIVE \(Delighter\).) Tj
T*
(   * Functional: 'I am neutral' AND Dysfunctional: 'I am neutral' -> INDIFFERENT \(Waste of time\).) Tj
T*
(   * Functional: 'I dislike it' AND Dysfunctional: 'I like it' -> REVERSE \(Harmful feature\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Strategic Roadmap Deployment:) Tj
T*
(   - Engineering releases must satisfy 100% of Must-be features, optimize competitive) Tj
T*
(   One-dimensional features, and include 1-2 Attractive delighters to conquer the market.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
