T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Three-Dimensional Evaluation Matrix:) Tj
T*
(   - Every candidate idea is scored on a standardized 1-to-5 scale across three core dimensions:) Tj
T*
(   * Desirability \(D - Product/UX\): Does the user want this? Does it solve an acute pain point?) Tj
T*
(   Will they use it?) Tj
T*
(   * Feasibility \(F - Engineering\): Can we build this with our current or near-term technology,) Tj
T*
(   infrastructure, and team skills within time constraints?) Tj
T*
(   * Viability \(V - Business/Finance\): Does it align with business models, regulatory compliance,) Tj
T*
(   unit economics, and profitability targets?) Tj
T*
(   - Composite Innovation Score = \(D * Weight_D\) + \(F * Weight_F\) + \(V * Weight_V\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Resolving Cross-Functional Conflicts:) Tj
T*
(   - Common Conflict Scenario: An idea scores 5 in Desirability \(users love it\), but 1 in) Tj
T*
