T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Shared High-Risk Context:) Tj
T*
(   - Both intensive care units \(ICUs\) and modern jet aircraft cockpits operate under extreme) Tj
T*
(   stress, where human operators manage complex, safety-critical multi-sensor telemetry under) Tj
T*
(   severe time constraints, where perceptual mistakes lead to loss of human life.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Aviation Ergonomics Adopted in ICU Dashboards:) Tj
T*
(   - The 'Dark Cockpit' Philosophy:) Tj
T*
(   * Aviation: Normal, stable flight systems emit zero colored lights or warnings; indicator) Tj
T*
(   lights ignite only when a system deviates from safe thresholds.) Tj
T*
(   * ICU Adoption: Patient monitors historically flashed hundreds of green and blue lights) Tj
T*
(   continuously, inducing sensory fatigue. Modern monitors remain visually calm, highlighting) Tj
T*
