(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the 'Six Thinking Hats' implementation rules. Why must the 'Red Hat' be strictly limited to 60 seconds per participant without requiring logical justification?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Procedural Execution Rules:) Tj
T*
(   - Discipline of Time Allocation: The facilitator maintains rigorous timeboxes for each hat:) Tj
T*
(   White Hat \(3-5 mins\), Black Hat \(4-5 mins\), Yellow Hat \(3-4 mins\), Green Hat \(5-8 mins\), Red) Tj
T*
(   Hat \(1 min total\).) Tj
T*
(   - Universal Directionality: Every single participant in the room must wear the same hat at the) Tj
T*
(   same time. No simultaneous cross-hat debates are permitted.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The 60-Second Rule for the Red Hat:) Tj
T*
(   - Visceral Emotional Authenticity: Intuition and gut feelings occur instantaneously in the) Tj
