(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze how 'Reverse Brainstorming' can be used during an architectural review to eliminate 'Single Points of Failure' \(SPOFs\) in a globally distributed e-commerce platform.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Reverse Brainstorming Protocol:) Tj
T*
(   - Challenge: 'How do we design our e-commerce platform so that Black Friday flash-sale traffic) Tj
T*
(   causes zero downtime and zero dropped orders?') Tj
T*
(   - Inverted Question: 'How could we design the platform so that a single component failure) Tj
T*
(   causes catastrophic total system blackout across all global regions?') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Reverse Ideas Generated by the Engineering Team:) Tj
T*
(   - Anti-Idea 1: 'Make all checkout transactions route through a single monolithic master SQL) Tj
T*
(   database located in Virginia, with zero local caching.') Tj
T*
(   * Implication & Remedy: Eliminate global database bottlenecks by deploying localized) Tj
T*
(   multi-region distributed databases \(CockroachDB/Spanner\) with regional replication.) Tj
T*
(   - Anti-Idea 2: 'Ensure that if our payment gateway provider suffers a network hiccup, the) Tj
T*
(   user's browser immediately crashes and empties their shopping cart.') Tj
T*
(   * Implication & Remedy: Implement asynchronous message queuing \(RabbitMQ/SQS\); if the payment) Tj
T*
(   gateway fails, buffer the transaction and display: 'Order Received, Processing Offline',) Tj
T*
(   decoupling checkout from external gateway latency.) Tj
T*
(   - Anti-Idea 3: 'Store all static frontend CSS, JavaScript, and product images on a single) Tj
T*
(   virtual machine without CDN edge caching.') Tj
T*
(   * Implication & Remedy: Deploy all static assets across globally distributed edge Content) Tj
T*
(   Delivery Networks \(Cloudflare/CloudFront\) with Origin Shield protection.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 28:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the role of 'Metaphorical Thinking' in software user interface design. How did the 'Desktop Metaphor' \(folders, trash cans, windows\) enable mass computer adoption?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Cognitive Function of Metaphors:) Tj
T*
(   - In cognitive linguistics \(Lakoff & Johnson\), metaphors allow humans to understand and) Tj
T*
(   structure a novel, abstract domain in terms of a familiar, concrete domain.) Tj
T*
(   - In early computing, operating systems required memorizing cryptic alphanumeric terminal) Tj
T*
(   commands \(`grep`, `chmod`, `rm -rf`\), confining computer use to specialized computer scientists) Tj
T*
(   and mathematicians.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Xerox PARC Desktop Metaphor \(1970s\):) Tj
T*
(   - Spatial Mapping: Mapped abstract hierarchical file systems \(inodes, pointers, magnetic disk) Tj
T*
(   sectors\) to familiar physical office objects:) Tj
T*
(   * A directory became a manila 'Folder'.) Tj
T*
(   * A data file became a white 'Document'.) Tj
T*
(   * Deleting a file became dragging it into a physical 'Trash Can'.) Tj
T*
(   * Concurrent multitasking became overlapping physical 'Windows' on an executive 'Desktop'.) Tj
T*
ET

